# M0 deliverable 5 — free-tier provider credentials (D14).
#
#   copy .env.example .env      then fill in whichever you have
#
# Every provider is OPTIONAL. The harness skips unconfigured ones rather than
# failing, so start with two: one primary, one secondary for the fallback chain.
# Get at least two — a chain with no secondary rung is not a chain.
#
# ⚠️ RSK-15 / D17 — READ THE DATA-USE TERMS FOR EACH PROVIDER YOU ENABLE.
# Free tiers commonly reserve the right to train on submitted content. That is a
# real problem for users' unpublished manuscripts, not a hypothetical. Record
# what each provider's policy actually says in SPIKE-FINDINGS.md; it decides
# whether `private_papers_local_only` defaults to on.

# --- Google Gemini (aistudio.google.com/apikey) ------------------------------
# Strong first candidate: long context, native JSON-schema output, generous
# daily limits.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash

# --- Groq (console.groq.com/keys) --------------------------------------------
# Very fast inference on open models; OpenAI-compatible API.
GROQ_API_KEY=
GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# --- Cerebras (cloud.cerebras.ai) -------------------------------------------
CEREBRAS_API_KEY=
CEREBRAS_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b

# --- OpenRouter (openrouter.ai/keys) ----------------------------------------
# Aggregator — useful as the SECOND provider so the eval judge can run on a
# different model family than the generator (RSK-4).
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free

# --- Mistral (console.mistral.ai) -------------------------------------------
MISTRAL_API_KEY=
MISTRAL_MODEL=mistral-small-latest

# --- OpenAI (platform.openai.com/api-keys) ----------------------------------
# ⚠️ PAID — no free tier. Conflicts with D14 unless credits already exist.
# Intended role is the EVAL JUDGE ONLY (offline, ~50 examples), not generation:
#   - sharpens judge-validation / Cohen's κ (RSK-4) without touching the hot path
#   - API data is NOT used for training by default, unlike Gemini's free tier (D29)
#   - supports strict json_schema, which Groq's Llama models reject (D28)
# Run 16_openai_probe.py before relying on it — a key can authenticate and still
# have zero quota, exactly as the Gemini credential did.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_JUDGE_MODEL=

# Model IDs above are starting guesses — free-tier catalogues change often.
# If a request 404s on the model name, list the provider's available models and
# update the value here rather than assuming the key is broken.
